#
# Counter-example for the math:Connection frame: a math:Connection
# naming NEITHER a math:CellularSheaf (via math:connectionOfSheaf, the discrete reading) NOR
# a math:Atlas/bundle (via math:connectionOn, the manifold reading) — a connection with no
# base to transport over. The min-1 qualified restriction on math:connectionOn derives a
# sh:qualifiedMinCount property shape, so validation MUST emit
# shacl.QualifiedMinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:IncompleteConnection).
# ISOLATION: the node is ONLY a math:Connection and declares no other property, so no other
# frame or constraint applies.
# Back-reference: math:IncompleteConnection (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecConnectionNoTransportRule).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:connection a math:Connection .        # names neither a sheaf nor an atlas — no math:connectionOn
